
Tried opentmux briefly, and it has 2 quick strikes against it.  I
followed the advice given on the web page and prompted qwen to
install opentmux, and it seemingly succesfully did so.  But the
installation wrote lines to the end of my ~/.bashrc, which in my
opinion is an utterly unacceptable practice.  Also, after the
install, the next time I opened opencode it connected to the wrong
model.  Installing a package should not change a person's already
established config.

That being said, I didn't use it enough to really form an opinion.
But it seems immature and not worth investigating further.
